<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>Etiuda</displayName>
  <description>Team folder and team lead's key</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_Etiuda">Etiuda</string>
      <string id="EtiudaCat">Etiuda</string>
      <string id="TeamFolder">Set the team folder</string>
      <string id="TeamFolder_Explain">This policy setting specifies the folder from which Etiuda reads the team file on this computer.

If you enable this policy setting, enter a full path, such as D:\Team\share or \\server\team. Etiuda reads the team file from this folder. A value that is not a full path is ignored, and Etiuda keeps the folder it already uses.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, the folder is chosen on the desk when it joins the team.

If both this setting and "Set the team lead's key" are configured and either value is not valid, Etiuda uses neither.</string>
      <string id="LeadKey">Set the team lead's key</string>
      <string id="LeadKey_Explain">This policy setting specifies the public key of the team lead whose team file Etiuda trusts on this computer.

If you enable this policy setting, enter the lead's public key as 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters, as it appears in the team file. Etiuda then trusts that key only: a team file signed with any other key is not used, including one handed over to a new lead. A value in any other form is ignored.

If you disable or do not configure this policy setting, Etiuda trusts the lead of the team the desk joined.

If both this setting and "Set the team folder" are configured and either value is not valid, Etiuda uses neither.</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="TeamFolder">
        <textBox refId="TeamFolderBox">
          <label>Full path:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="LeadKey">
        <textBox refId="LeadKeyBox">
          <label>Public key (64 lowercase hexadecimal characters):</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
